<title>USA: Government seeks more information on Boeing merger.</title>
<headline>Government seeks more information on Boeing merger.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Trade Commission has asked Boeing Co for more information to consider its request to merge with McDonnell-Douglas, a Boeing spokeswoman said Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We've been asked to provide a variety of documents to the FTC and will fully cooperate with that request,&quot; said Sherry Nebel at company headquarters in Seattle.</p>
<p>Boeing and McDonnell-Douglas made their original filing with the FTC earlier this year. Boeing officials have predicted they will win approval from the government for the merger later this year.</p>
